E
"go1"
"You crouch just inside the copse of trees the old warrior mentioned, stopping
a moment to examine your surroundings.
"
E
"go2"
"The copse is dense.  A bird has nested in the branches just above you.  Past
the trees to the north, a fire blazes in a clearing.
"
E
"go3"
"It is night.  The alyoshins sit beside the fire, feasting upon turkey, wild
roots, and wine.  The warlord, marked by a dark crown, sit among the more than
thirty present at the council.
"
E
"go4"
"The moon is high overhead.  A pair of drummers beat on tall, deep drums.  A
pair of guards patrol the circle.
"
E
"go5"
"You seem to have arrived in the middle of an argument.
"
E
"go6"
"@g\"Why do we not march on Sos-Kul?\"@n One of the bearded men asks.@g \"We are ready.
The men are ready.  They grow anxious and tire of patrols.\"
"
E
"go7"
"The warlord chews upon a greasy drumstick.  @B\"The lizardmen are not our
enemies, Vilka.\"@n He stares unconcernedly at the younger, yet venerable,
warrior.
"
E
"go8"
"@g \"Not our enemies!?\" @nOne of the alyoshins has jumped to his feet.  @g\"All the
city-born are our enemies!  Have you forgotten how they cast us out?  Set the
wolves upon us and cursed us?\"
"
E
"go9"
"@y\"Aye, aye,\" @nthe other councilmen grunt in assent.
"
E
"go10"
"@g\"And when they found our villages, they set upon them, setting them to fire,
murdered our women and again chased us out of our homes!\"@n
"
E
"go11"
"@y\"Aye, aye!\"@n The clamoring grows louder.
"
E
"go12"
"One of the guards approaches the copse of trees within which you stand.  You
shrink back against the trunk of a tree, trying to evade his lupine gaze.
"
E
"go13"
"The argument continues in the background.  Some of the alyoshins are gesturing
an shouting as the discussion heats up.
"
E
"go14"
"The guard approaches the very tree you stand against.
"
E
"go15"
"A loud drum beat shakes your chest.  The night above presses down upon you.
"
E
"go16"
"You can hear the guard's breath as he creeps closer to the tree.
"
E
"go17"
"A branch snaps as the guard steps just up to the tree.
"
E
"go18"
"@G\"Ridddddddatwilatalatalatalabrrrrdrdrdrdrr!\"@n the bird above you sings out.
You hear the guard behind you shuffle and grunt in agitation.  You wait until
the sound of him walking away disappears until you return, relieved, to your
watch of the council.
"
